# PowOS layer on Android: which of the Containerfile's `staging` COPY sources go into the phone rootfs.
#
# HACK: this list duplicates the Containerfile's staging stage instead of sharing it, so that adding
# the phone target changes NOTHING in the desktop / Steam Deck image build. check-layer-drift.sh
# fails when the Containerfile gains a source this file doesn't account for. Real fix (later, once
# the phone build is proven): one manifest both builds read.
#
# Format:  + <source> <destination>    copy into the rootfs
#          - <source> <reason>         not on Android, on purpose
# Sources are relative to the repo root, exactly as written in the Containerfile.

+ bin/                                  /usr/bin/
+ lib/                                  /usr/lib/powos/
+ desktop/plasmoid/                     /usr/share/plasma/plasmoids/
+ desktop/autostart/                    /etc/xdg/autostart/
+ config/kde/powermanagementprofilesrc  /etc/xdg/powermanagementprofilesrc
+ config/kde/kglobalshortcutsrc         /etc/xdg/kglobalshortcutsrc
+ config/kde/kwinrc                     /etc/xdg/kwinrc
+ config/kde/kdeglobals                 /etc/xdg/kdeglobals
+ config/kde/konsolerc                  /etc/xdg/konsolerc
+ config/kde/konsole/                   /usr/share/konsole/
+ config/kde/plasma-env/                /etc/xdg/plasma-workspace/env/
+ config/ai/                            /etc/powos/ai/
+ config/zones/                         /etc/powos/zones/
+ config/skel/                          /etc/skel/
+ config/etc/profile.d/                 /etc/profile.d/
+ config/tmux/tmux.conf                 /etc/tmux.conf
+ .snapshot/                            /usr/lib/powos/src/

- config/sddm.conf.d/                   no display manager: the Android app starts the session
- config/etc/systemd/logind.conf.d/60-powos-deck-power.conf  no logind on Android
- config/ublue-os/motd/powos.md         Bazzite's MOTD renderer is not in the Arch rootfs
- config/logid/logid.cfg                Logitech daemon needs /dev/hidraw, which apps can't open
- config/tmpfiles.d/                    no systemd-tmpfiles on Android
- config/dracut.conf.d/95-powos-deck-slim.conf  no initramfs: Android boots its own kernel
- config/systemd-preset/                no systemd on Android
- config/sysctl.d/                      the kernel is Android's; apps can't set sysctls
- config/NetworkManager/conf.d/         Android owns the network (android-nm is a stand-in)
- config/etc/containers/systemd/users/  Quadlets need systemd + user namespaces (denied to apps)
- config/etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/         no sshd yet (would need a non-privileged port; later)
- config/etc/ssh/authorized_keys.d/     no sshd yet
- config/etc/systemd/logind.conf.d/     no logind on Android
- config/etc/containers/oci/hooks.d/    podman can't run in an Android app (no namespaces)
- config/etc/containers/containers.conf.d/  same
- config/etc/environment.d/             read by systemd --user only
- systemd/greeter-watchdog.service      no display manager / greeter
- systemd/greeter-watchdog.timer        same
- systemd/plasmalogin.service.d/        same
- systemd/sddm.service.d/               same
- systemd/plymouth-quit.service.d/      no boot splash: Android boots the phone
- systemd/plymouth-quit-wait.service.d/ same
- systemd/cardwired.service.d/          no systemd on Android
- systemd/NetworkManager-wait-online.service.d/  same
- systemd/greenboot-healthcheck.service.d/  same (and no bootc deployments to roll back)
- systemd/bootloader-update.service.d/  no bootloader: an app never boots
- systemd/powos-firstboot.service       the app's first-boot hook replaces it (session/first-boot.sh)
- systemd/powos-variant-retry.service   GPU variants are x86 desktop-only
- systemd/powos-installer.service       no disk installer on a phone app
- systemd/powos-safemode.service        boot modes need a bootloader
- systemd/powos-boot-entries.service    same
- systemd/powos-firstboot-notice.service  same as powos-firstboot
- systemd/powos-initramfs-slim.service  no initramfs
